course: dictionary
lesson: 2618
title: Descend: three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Descend is a verb, and it means to go or come down, or to move downwards. Planes descend to land, and climbers descend a mountain. The clue is the direction: something is going down.
explain: Descend has two more meanings you will meet in history and family stories. «City pigeons are descended from wild rock doves» means the pigeons come from those birds in their family line, like great-great-grandchildren come from their ancestors. «The whole countryside descending on him» means a crowd arriving suddenly.
explain: To choose the right meaning, swap your idea into the sentence and see if it still makes sense. Ask: is something going down, does something come from someone, or do lots of people arrive at once?
fact: Descend is a verb: descend, descends, descended, descending.
fact: «Descend» means to go or come down, or to move downwards.
fact: «Descended from» means to come from someone in your family history.
fact: «Descend on» a place means to arrive there suddenly in large numbers.
fact: «Descending order» means a list from the biggest to the smallest, such as 9, 7, 4, 2.
exercise: «The climbers began to descend the mountain before the storm.» What does descend mean here? | Climb up | *Go down | Fall asleep | Sing loudly
exercise: «Most Jamaicans today descend from Africans enslaved on British plantations.» What does descend from mean? | Work on a plantation | Live next door to them | Move to a new country tomorrow | *Come from them in family history
exercise: «Put the numbers in descending order: 9, 7, 4, 2.» What does descending order mean? | In alphabetical order | *From biggest to smallest | From smallest to biggest | Written in red ink
test: «The lift will descend to the ground floor.» Which word means the same as descend here? | Go round | Go away | Go up | *Go down
test: «Modern Chinese characters descend from Shang writing.» Which meaning of descend is used? | Go down a hill | *Come from it in history | Lower the volume | Arrive suddenly in large numbers
exam: «City pigeons are descended from wild rock doves.» Which meaning of descend is used in this sentence? | Fly away quickly | Go down a cliff | *Come from them in family history | Arrive in large numbers
